      "name": "CopyUnicodeString",
      "signature": "short * CopyUnicodeString(short * pwszDest, short * pwszSource, int nMaxChars)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "short *",
      "comment": "Copy Unicode (wide-character) string with null padding.\n\nCopies up to nMaxChars wide characters from source to destination buffer.\nIf the source string terminates before nMaxChars, the remaining buffer\nspace is zero-filled (null-padded).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize destination pointer and remaining count\n2. Copy loop: Copy 16-bit characters from source to destination\n   - Decrement count each iteration\n   - Stop if source null terminator reached or count exhausted\n3. Null-padding loop: If count remains, zero-fill using REP STOSD/STOSW\n   - Use STOSD for bulk 4-byte writes (2 chars at a time)\n   - Use STOSW for remaining odd character if needed\n4. Return original destination pointer\n\nParameters:\n  pwszDest (short* in ECX): Destination buffer for wide string (IMPLICIT)\n  pwszSource (short* in EDX): Source wide string to copy (IMPLICIT)\n  nMaxChars (int on stack): Maximum characters to copy/buffer size\n\nReturns:\n  short*: Pointer to destination buffer (original pwszDest value)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If nMaxChars is 0, no copy occurs\n  - If source is shorter than nMaxChars, remaining space is null-padded\n  - Null terminator in source stops copying but not padding\n\nAssembly Optimization:\n  - Uses REP STOSD for fast 4-byte null padding\n  - Uses REP STOSW for final 2-byte word if odd count\n  - Optimized for wide (16-bit) character strings\n\nMangled Name: ?strncpy@Unicode@@SIPAU1@PAU1@PBU1@H@Z",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
