      "name": "strstri",
      "signature": "Unicode * strstri(Unicode * pwszHaystack, Unicode * pwszNeedle)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "Unicode *",
      "comment": "Case-insensitive substring search for Unicode (wide character) strings.\nSearches pwszHaystack for the first occurrence of pwszNeedle, comparing\ncharacters case-insensitively using a lookup table for ASCII characters.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate both pointers are non-NULL, return NULL if either is NULL\n2. Load first characters from haystack and needle\n3. Convert both to lowercase using g_awToLowerTable (for chars < 0x100)\n4. If first chars don't match, advance haystack and retry from step 2\n5. When first chars match, enter inner comparison loop\n6. Compare remaining needle chars against haystack (case-insensitive)\n7. If mismatch found before needle end, backtrack and continue outer search\n8. If needle fully matched, return pointer to match start in haystack\n9. If haystack exhausted before needle matched, return NULL\n\nParameters:\npwszHaystack (ECX) - Unicode string to search within (haystack)\npwszNeedle (EDX) - Unicode substring to find (needle)\n\nReturns:\nPointer to first occurrence of needle in haystack (case-insensitive match)\nNULL if needle not found or if either input pointer is NULL\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Returns NULL immediately if pwszHaystack is NULL\n- Returns NULL immediately if pwszNeedle is NULL\n- Characters >= 0x100 are compared directly without case conversion\n- Characters < 0x100 use g_awToLowerTable for lowercase conversion\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x100 - ASCII range threshold for case conversion table lookup\n0x6fc4d2fc (g_awToLowerTable) - 256-entry Unicode lowercase conversion table",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:5a933e96c7627f81558b63712cf4806e3eff599c3940703ab73ff8656dd399ea",
