      "name": "directionality",
      "signature": "Direction directionality(void * this, ushort * param_1)",
      "calling_convention": "__thiscall",
      "return_type": "Direction",
      "comment": "Determines text direction (LTR/RTL/neutral) of character.\\n\\nAlgorithm:\\n1. Check character code point against known ranges\\n2. Return direction enum value:\\n   - 0xF0 = Left-to-Right (Latin, CJK, etc.)\\n   - 0xF1 = Right-to-Left (Hebrew, Arabic, etc.)\\n   - 0xF2 = Neutral (most punctuation, unknowns)\\n\\nParameters:\\n  this (Unicode*): Pointer to Unicode object instance\\n\\nReturns:\\n  Direction: Enum value (0xF0=LTR, 0xF1=RTL, 0xF2=Neutral)\\n\\nUnicode Ranges:\\n  RTL (0xF1): 0x590-0x8FF (Semitic scripts)\\n  LTR (0xF0): 0x30-0x39, 0x40-0x5A, 0x61-0x7A (ASCII alphanumeric)\\n             0xC0-0x58F (Latin Extended)\\n             0x900-0x10FF (Indic scripts)\\n             0x3040-0x8BFF (CJK, Japanese, Korean)\\n  Special: 0x200E (LTR mark), 0x200F (RTL mark)\\n\\nNotes:\\n  - Mangled name: ?directionality@Unicode@@QAE?AW4Direction@1@XZ",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
