      "name": "loadSysMap",
      "signature": "int loadSysMap(HD2ARCHIVE__ * pArchive, char * lpszFilePath)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Loads system-to-Unicode character mapping tables from a KAMAP archive file.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load archive file and verify \"KAMAP\" signature (5-byte magic)\n2. Parse header scanning for 0x1A terminator (max 40 chars version string)\n3. Tokenize version/charset info string using delimiter\n4. Allocate and copy byte range table (single-byte char ranges)\n5. Allocate forward mapping table (system char -> Unicode pairs)\n6. Allocate reverse mapping table (Unicode -> system lookups)\n7. Store charset name and entry counts in global variables\n\nParameters:\n  pArchive (HD2ARCHIVE__*): ECX - Handle to open archive containing mapping file\n  lpszFilePath (char*): EDX - Path to KAMAP file within archive\n\nReturns:\n  int: 1 on successful load, 0 on failure (signature mismatch, header overflow,\n       allocation failure)\n\nFile Format (KAMAP):\n  Offset  Size  Description\n  0x00    5     \"KAMAP\" signature\n  0x05    1     Start of version string\n  ...     var   Version string until 0x1A terminator (max 40 bytes)\n  +0      2     wMappingCount - number of char mapping entries\n  +2      1     bRangeCount - number of byte ranges\n  +3      var   Byte range table: bRangeCount * 2 bytes (min/max pairs)\n  +var    var   Forward map: wMappingCount * 4 bytes (sys_char:2, unicode:2)\n  +var    var   Reverse map: wMappingCount * 2 bytes (sorted for lookup)\n\nGlobals Modified:\n  g_pByteRangeTable (0x6fc50bc0): Pointer to byte range min/max pairs\n  g_pSysToUnicodeMap (0x6fc50bbc): Forward mapping table (sys->unicode)\n  g_pUnicodeToSysMap (0x6fc50bec): Reverse mapping table (unicode->sys)\n  g_wMappingEntryCount (0x6fc50bb8): Number of mapping entries\n  g_bByteRangeCount (0x6fc50bf0): Number of byte ranges\n\nError Handling:\n  - Line 0x69: Signature mismatch (not \"KAMAP\")\n  - Line 0x7D: Header too long (>40 chars before 0x1A)\n  - Line 0x95: Byte range table allocation failed\n  - Line 0xA2: Forward mapping allocation failed\n  - Line 0xB4: Reverse mapping allocation failed\n\nMemory Management:\n  - Frees existing tables before reallocating (prevents leaks)\n  - Uses SMemAlloc/SMemFree for Storm memory pool\n  - All allocations from \"new[]\" pool marker\n\nMangled: ?loadSysMap@Unicode@@SIHPAUHD2ARCHIVE__@@PBD@Z",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
