      "name": "sys2Unicode",
      "signature": "Unicode * sys2Unicode(Unicode * pDstUnicode, char * szSrcSysStr, int nMaxChars)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "Unicode *",
      "comment": "Converts system charset string to Unicode using loaded character mapping tables.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if character mapping is loaded (g_pUnicodeToSysMap != NULL)\n2. If no mapping loaded, delegate to win2Unicode for Windows codepage conversion\n3. For each source byte until null terminator or nMaxChars reached:\n   a. If byte < 0x20, treat as control character and copy as-is (single byte)\n   b. Check if byte falls within single-byte ranges defined in g_pByteRangeTable\n   c. If in single-byte range, convert directly; otherwise read 2 bytes as DBCS character\n4. For characters >= 0x20, perform binary search in mapping table:\n   a. Use g_wMappingEntryCount to determine search bounds\n   b. Binary search g_pUnicodeToSysMap index to find matching entry\n   c. Look up Unicode value from g_pSysToUnicodeMap at found index\n5. Store converted Unicode character in destination buffer\n6. If source ends with null and space remains, null-terminate destination\n\nParameters:\n  pDstUnicode (Unicode*): ECX - Destination buffer for Unicode output\n  szSrcSysStr (char*): EDX - Source string in system charset encoding\n  nMaxChars (int): Stack - Maximum number of characters to convert\n\nReturns:\n  Unicode*: Pointer to destination buffer (pDstUnicode)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Returns immediately via win2Unicode if no mapping table loaded\n  - Null terminator in source stops conversion early\n  - Control characters (< 0x20) passed through unchanged\n  - DBCS lead bytes trigger 2-byte read for double-byte character sets\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x20 - ASCII space, threshold between control chars and printable\n  0xff - Mask for byte range count extraction\n  0xffff - Mask for mapping entry count extraction\n  4 - Size of mapping table entry (2 bytes sys code + 2 bytes Unicode)\n\nMangled: ?sys2Unicode@Unicode@@SIPAU1@PAU1@PBDH@Z",
