      "name": "unicode2Sys",
      "signature": "char * unicode2Sys(char * szDest, Unicode * pUnicodeSrc, int nMaxChars)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "char *",
      "comment": "Converts a Unicode string to the system charset using the loaded character mapping table.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if system-to-Unicode mapping table is loaded (g_pSysToUnicodeMap)\n2. If no mapping loaded, fall back to unicode2Win for Windows codepage conversion\n3. For each Unicode character in source string until null or nMaxChars reached:\n   a. If character < 0x20 (control char), copy directly as single byte\n   b. Otherwise, look up character in reverse mapping via BinarySearchArray\n   c. If found in mapping, extract the system charset byte(s)\n   d. For single-byte chars (high byte == 0): check byte range table for DBCS lead bytes\n   e. For DBCS chars or out-of-range: write high byte first, then low byte\n   f. For single-byte in valid range: write only the low byte\n4. If source string ends with null and space permits, append null terminator\n5. Return pointer to destination buffer\n\nParameters:\n  szDest (char*): ECX - Destination buffer for system charset string\n  pUnicodeSrc (Unicode*): EDX - Source Unicode string pointer\n  nMaxChars (int): Stack[0x4] - Maximum number of characters to convert\n\nReturns:\n  char*: Pointer to szDest (destination buffer)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Returns unicode2Win result if no mapping table loaded\n  - Handles DBCS (Double-Byte Character Set) encoding\n  - Control characters (< 0x20) bypass mapping lookup\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x20 - ASCII space, threshold for control characters\n  0x4 - Size of mapping entry (2 bytes Unicode + 2 bytes system)\n\nStructure Layout (Mapping Entry):\n  Offset  Size  Field       Type    Description\n  0x00    2     wSysChar    ushort  System charset character code\n  0x02    2     wUnicode    ushort  Unicode character code\n\nRelated Globals:\n  g_pSysToUnicodeMap - Pointer to Unicode-to-system mapping array\n  g_wMappingEntryCount - Number of entries in mapping table\n  g_pByteRangeTable - DBCS lead byte range table\n  g_bByteRangeCount - Number of byte range entries\n\nMangled Name: ?unicode2Sys@Unicode@@SIPADPADPBU1@H@Z",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
