      "name": "sysWidth",
      "signature": "ulong sysWidth(Unicode * pUnicodeStr, int nMaxChars)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "ulong",
      "comment": "Calculates the byte width of a Unicode string when converted to the system charset.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if system-to-Unicode mapping table (g_pSysToUnicodeMap) is loaded\n2. If no mapping exists, fall back to strlen() for simple byte counting\n3. Initialize byte width counter to zero\n4. For each Unicode character (up to nMaxChars):\n   a. Read current 16-bit Unicode character\n   b. If null terminator, return accumulated width\n   c. If control char (< 0x20), skip lookup and check directly\n   d. Otherwise, search mapping table via BinarySearchArray()\n   e. Determine if mapped value is single-byte or double-byte:\n      - High byte zero AND low byte < 0x20: add 1 (control char)\n      - High byte zero: scan g_pByteRangeTable for DBCS lead byte ranges\n      - If in lead byte range: add 1 (single-byte char)\n      - Otherwise: add 2 (double-byte or unmapped char)\n5. Return total byte width\n\nParameters:\n  pUnicodeStr (Unicode*): ECX - Pointer to Unicode string to measure\n  nMaxChars (int): EDX - Maximum number of Unicode characters to process\n\nReturns:\n  ulong: Total bytes needed to represent string in system charset\n         Falls back to strlen() result if no mapping table loaded\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - No mapping table: Returns strlen(unaff_EDI) - appears to use EDI as fallback\n  - Null terminator: Returns accumulated width immediately\n  - Control chars (< 0x20): Treated as single-byte\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x20 - ASCII space, boundary for control characters\n  0x4  - Size of mapping table entry (2 bytes Unicode + 2 bytes system)\n\nRelated Globals:\n  g_pSysToUnicodeMap (0x6fc50bbc) - Pointer to Unicode-to-system mapping table\n  g_wMappingEntryCount (0x6fc50bb8) - Number of entries in mapping table\n  g_pByteRangeTable (0x6fc50bc0) - DBCS lead byte range table\n  g_bByteRangeCount (0x6fc50bf0) - Number of byte range entries\n\nMangled: ?sysWidth@Unicode@@SIKPBU1@H@Z",
