      "name": "CalculateUnicodeDisplayWidth",
      "signature": "ulong CalculateUnicodeDisplayWidth(char * lpszString, int nMaxBytes)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "ulong",
      "comment": "Calculates the display width of a Unicode string accounting for double-width characters.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if Unicode-to-system character map is loaded (g_pUnicodeToSysMap)\n2. If no map loaded, fall back to strlen using SCASB.REPNE instruction\n3. Otherwise iterate through string bytes up to nMaxBytes limit\n4. For each character:\n   a. If null terminator found, exit loop\n   b. If control character (< 0x20), count as single width\n   c. Check against g_pByteRangeTable to determine if double-width\n   d. Increment display width by 2 for double-width, 1 for single-width\n5. Return total display width\n\nParameters:\n  lpszString (ECX) - Pointer to null-terminated string to measure\n  nMaxBytes (EDX) - Maximum number of bytes to process\n\nReturns:\n  Display width of string in character cells (double-width chars count as 2)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Returns strlen if no system character map is loaded\n  - Control characters (< 0x20) always count as single-width\n  - Null terminator ends processing before nMaxBytes limit\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x20 - ASCII space, characters below are control codes\n  0xFF - Mask for byte range count extraction",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:08f94ae6c60eac43488e1aeafbf17517c28ff94c0288a3fee8eba577a635709d",
