      "name": "toUnicode",
      "signature": "Unicode * toUnicode(Unicode * pDstBuffer, char * lpszSrcUtf8, int nMaxChars)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "Unicode *",
      "comment": "Converts a UTF-8 encoded string to Unicode (UTF-16LE).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calculate source string length using REPNE SCASB\n2. Initialize output and input indices to 0\n3. For each UTF-8 sequence until max output chars reached:\n   a. Get lead byte and calculate bytes remaining in source\n   b. Look up lead byte in g_pUtf8EncodingTable encoding table\n   c. Match mask pattern to determine sequence length (1-4 bytes)\n   d. For multi-byte sequences, validate continuation bytes (must be 10xxxxxx)\n   e. Accumulate codepoint by shifting and ORing 6-bit continuation values\n   f. Validate codepoint is >= minimum for sequence length (prevents overlong)\n   g. Store 16-bit codepoint in destination buffer\n4. Null-terminate the destination buffer\n5. Return pointer to destination buffer\n\nParameters:\n  pDstBuffer (Unicode*): ECX - Destination buffer for Unicode output\n  lpszSrcUtf8 (char*): EDX - Source UTF-8 encoded null-terminated string\n  nMaxChars (int): Stack - Maximum number of 16-bit characters to write\n\nReturns:\n  Unicode*: Pointer to destination buffer (same as pDstBuffer)\n\nUTF-8 Encoding Table (g_pUtf8EncodingTable):\n  Offset  Size  Field         Description\n  0x00    2     wMask         Bit mask for lead byte matching\n  0x02    2     wSignature    Expected bits after masking\n  0x04    4     dwDataMask    Mask to extract codepoint bits\n  0x08    4     nMinValue     Minimum valid codepoint for length\n\nUTF-8 Byte Patterns:\n  0xxxxxxx - 1-byte sequence (ASCII, U+0000-U+007F)\n  110xxxxx 10xxxxxx - 2-byte sequence (U+0080-U+07FF)\n  1110xxxx 10xxxxxx 10xxxxxx - 3-byte sequence (U+0800-U+FFFF)\n  11110xxx 10xxxxxx 10xxxxxx 10xxxxxx - 4-byte sequence (U+10000-U+10FFFF)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Empty source string returns immediately with null-terminated buffer\n  - Invalid continuation byte (not 10xxxxxx) terminates decoding\n  - Overlong sequences (codepoint < min for length) terminate decoding\n  - Buffer overflow protection via nMaxChars limit\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0xFFFFFFFF - Initial counter for REPNE SCASB strlen\n  0x80 - XOR value to check continuation byte pattern\n  0xC0 - AND mask to isolate continuation byte marker bits\n  6 - Shift amount for accumulating continuation bytes\n  16 (0x10) - Table entry stride in bytes\n\nMangled Name: ?toUnicode@Unicode@@SIPAU1@PAU1@PBDH@Z",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
