      "name": "toUtf",
      "signature": "char * toUtf(char * lpszOutput, Unicode * pUnicodeInput, int nMaxBytes)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "char *",
      "comment": "Converts a Unicode (UTF-16) string to UTF-8 encoded string.\n\nThis function processes each Unicode codepoint from the input buffer and\nencodes it using the UTF-8 variable-length encoding scheme, utilizing\ng_pUtf8EncodingTable to determine the appropriate byte sequence.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if input string is empty (null character check at start)\n2. Initialize output index to 0, prepare to iterate source characters\n3. For each Unicode character while output space remains:\n   a. Extract current codepoint as 16-bit unsigned value\n   b. Search g_pUtf8EncodingTable for matching encoding entry\n   c. Calculate lead byte: (codepoint >> shift) | prefix_mask\n   d. Write lead byte to output buffer\n   e. Write continuation bytes: ((codepoint >> (shift-6)) & 0x3F) | 0x80\n   f. Advance input pointer by 2 bytes (sizeof Unicode char)\n   g. Increment output index by byte count\n4. Null-terminate the output buffer at final position\n5. Return pointer to output buffer\n\nParameters:\n  lpszOutput (char*): ECX - Destination buffer for UTF-8 encoded string\n  pUnicodeInput (Unicode*): EDX - Source Unicode (UTF-16) null-terminated string\n  nMaxBytes (int): Stack[0x4] - Maximum bytes to write (prevents buffer overflow)\n\nReturns:\n  char*: Pointer to lpszOutput destination buffer (always returns input buffer)\n\nUTF-8 Encoding Table Structure (16 bytes per entry at g_pUtf8EncodingTable):\n  Offset 0x0: ushort - Sentinel value (0 = end of table marker)\n  Offset 0x2: byte - Lead byte prefix mask (0x00, 0xC0, or 0xE0)\n  Offset 0x4: short - Initial right-shift amount (0, 6, or 12 bits)\n  Offset 0x8: int - Maximum codepoint threshold for this encoding\n\nUTF-8 Byte Patterns Generated:\n  1-byte: 0xxxxxxx (ASCII range 0x00-0x7F) - shift=0, prefix=0x00\n  2-byte: 110xxxxx 10xxxxxx (range 0x80-0x7FF) - shift=6, prefix=0xC0\n  3-byte: 1110xxxx 10xxxxxx 10xxxxxx (range 0x800-0xFFFF) - shift=12, prefix=0xE0\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Empty input (null at start): Returns immediately with empty output string\n  - Encoding table entry not found: Exits encoding loop early\n  - Output buffer limit reached: Stops before exceeding nMaxBytes-1 bytes\n\nNotes:\n  - Static member function of Unicode class using __fastcall convention\n  - C++ Mangled name: ?toUtf@Unicode@@SIPADPADPBU1@H@Z\n  - Uses global encoding table at address 0x6fc4d758\n  - Ordinal 10052 in export table",
