      "name": "IsBindingStateFlagSet",
      "signature": "dword IsBindingStateFlagSet(void * this, int param_1)",
      "calling_convention": "__thiscall",
      "return_type": "dword",
      "comment": "Check if binding state flag (0x8) is set\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Compare g_dwBindingMode with 1\n2. If g_dwBindingMode > 1: Call FUN_6fb9f44c(pThis, nBindingIndex, 8) and return result\n3. If g_dwBindingMode <= 1: Read byte from g_pBindingStates[nBindingIndex * 2], AND with 0x8, return result\n\nParameters:\n- pThis (void*): Object instance (ECX register)\n- nBindingIndex (int): Index into binding state array\n\nReturns:\n- Non-zero if flag 0x8 is set in binding state\n- Zero if flag is not set\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Two code paths depending on g_dwBindingMode value\n- Direct array access when binding mode <= 1\n- Delegates to FUN_6fb9f44c for binding mode > 1\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 1: Binding mode threshold\n- 8 (0x8): Flag bit being tested\n- 2: Array stride multiplier (word access pattern)",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
