      "name": "CleanupMemoryDescriptors",
      "signature": "void CleanupMemoryDescriptors(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Cleanup all allocated memory descriptors and destroy the global heap.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if any descriptors exist (g_nDescriptorCount > 0)\n2. If descriptors exist, iterate through the descriptor array\n3. For each descriptor, perform memory cleanup:\n   - Release virtual memory with MEM_DECOMMIT (0x4000) for 1MB region\n   - Release virtual memory with MEM_RELEASE (0x8000) to fully free\n   - Free associated heap memory using the global heap handle\n4. Advance to next descriptor (20-byte stride)\n5. Continue until all descriptors processed\n6. Free the descriptor array itself from the global heap\n7. Destroy the global heap handle\n\nParameters:\nNone (void function)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\nIf g_nDescriptorCount is 0 or negative, skips cleanup loop and proceeds directly to heap destruction\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x4000 - MEM_DECOMMIT flag for VirtualFree (decommit pages)\n0x8000 - MEM_RELEASE flag for VirtualFree (release address space)\n0x100000 - 1MB size parameter for VirtualFree decommit operation\n0xC - Offset to first descriptor (12 bytes from array base)\n0x14 - Descriptor stride (20 bytes per MemoryDescriptor)\n\nStructure Layout:\nMemoryDescriptor (20 bytes):\nOffset Size Field Name     Type    Description\n0x00   4    pVirtualMemory void*   Virtual memory address for VirtualFree\n0x04   4    pHeapMemory    void*   Heap memory address for HeapFree\n0x08   4    dwReserved1    uint    Reserved field 1\n0x0C   4    dwReserved2    uint    Reserved field 2\n0x10   4    dwReserved3    uint    Reserved field 3",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
