      "comment": "Sets or queries the current locale for a specific category.\n\n  This is the C runtime setlocale() implementation. When szLocale is NULL,\n  returns the current locale string for the category. When szLocale is\n  provided, sets the locale and returns the new locale string.\n\n  Algorithm:\n    1. Validate nCategory is in range 0-5 (0x0-0x5)\n    2. Acquire critical section 0x13 for thread safety\n    3. Increment g_bSyncFlag and wait for g_dwThreadRefCount == 0\n    4. If nCategory == 0 (LC_ALL):\n       a. If szLocale is NULL, build combined locale string via BuildLocaleString\n       b. If szLocale starts with \"LC_\", parse compound format (LC_COLLATE=X;LC_CTYPE=Y;...)\n       c. Otherwise parse simple locale and apply to all categories\n    5. If nCategory != 0:\n       a. If szLocale is NULL, return current locale for that category\n       b. Otherwise set locale for specific category via SetSingleLocale\n    6. Release critical section and decrement g_bSyncFlag\n\n  Parameters:\n    nCategory  - Locale category constant:\n                 0 = LC_ALL, 1 = LC_COLLATE, 2 = LC_CTYPE,\n                 3 = LC_MONETARY, 4 = LC_NUMERIC, 5 = LC_TIME\n    szLocale   - Locale string to set, or NULL to query current\n\n  Returns:\n    Pointer to current locale string on success\n    NULL on failure or invalid category\n\n  Special Cases:\n    - Category out of range (< 0 or > 5): Returns NULL immediately\n    - NULL szLocale with LC_ALL: Builds combined \"LC_xxx=value;...\" string\n    - Compound \"LC_xxx=value;...\" format: Parses and sets each category",
