      "name": "ParseCodecParameters",
      "signature": "int ParseCodecParameters(char * szOutput, byte * pszInput)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Parses codec parameters from delimited input string into output buffer sections.\n  \n  Algorithm:\n    1. Zero-fill output buffer (0x88 = 136 bytes total)\n    2. Check if input starts with \".\" (0x2e):\n       - If standalone \".\" only, copy remainder to section 2 and return success\n       - Otherwise continue to main parse loop\n    3. Main loop: scan input for tokens delimited by \".\", \"_\", or \",\" (0x5f, 0x2c)\n       - Call FUN_00409400 to find next token boundary\n       - Based on section index (0/1/2), copy token to corresponding offset:\n         * Section 0 (offset 0x00): max 0x40 (64) bytes, reject if contains \".\"\n         * Section 1 (offset 0x40): max 0x40 bytes, reject if contains \"_\"\n         * Section 2 (offset 0x80): accept only null or \",\" terminator\n    4. Advance to next token and repeat until comma or null encountered\n  \n  Parameters:\n    [EBP+0x8] pbOutput - Output buffer, 0x88 (136) bytes (three 0x40-byte sections)\n    [EBP+0xc] pbInput - Input string with codec parameter delimiters\n  \n  Returns:\n    EAX = 0x00000000: Successful parse (comma or null terminator reached)\n    EAX = 0xffffffff: Error (token exceeds max length, invalid delimiter for section)",
