      "comment": "Validates all locale-specific codec configuration fields by querying locale information.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Check if pCodecData is NULL; return 0xFFFFFFFF (failure) if so\n  2. Load global locale identifier from g_dwCodecLocale into local register\n  3. For each string pointer field (offsets 0xC-0x24):\n     - Call GetLocaleInfoByType with mode=1 (string mode) and locale type ID\n     - Accumulate error results via bitwise OR\n  4. Call SanitizeNumericString on field at +0x1C to remove non-numeric characters\n  5. For each byte field (offsets 0x28-0x2F):\n     - Call GetLocaleInfoByType with mode=0 (byte mode) and locale type ID\n     - Accumulate error results via bitwise OR\n  6. Return combined error state (0=success, 0xFFFFFFFF=any field failed)\n\nParameters:\n  pCodecData [ESP+0x4]  Pointer to CodecData structure (172 bytes) containing\n                        locale-specific codec configuration fields to validate\n\nReturns:\n  0x00000000  All codec parameter fields validated successfully\n  0xFFFFFFFF  One or more fields failed validation (OR of all error flags)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - NULL pointer input immediately returns 0xFFFFFFFF\n  - Field at offset +0x1C is additionally sanitized after validation\n  - String fields use mode=1; byte fields use mode=0\n\nField Mapping (Locale Type IDs):\n  Offset  Type ID  Mode  Description\n  0x0C    0x15     1     String field 3 (pField3)\n  0x10    0x14     1     String field 4 (pField4)\n  0x14    0x16     1     String field 5 (pField5)\n  0x18    0x17     1     String field 6 (pField6)\n  0x1C    0x18     1     String field 7 (pField7) - sanitized\n  0x20    0x50     1     String field 8 (pField8)\n  0x24    0x51     1     String field 9 (pField9)\n  0x28    0x1A     0     Byte field 10 (pField10[0])\n  0x29    0x19     0     Byte field 10+1\n  0x2A    0x54     0     Byte field 10+2\n  0x2B    0x55     0     Byte field 10+3\n  0x2C    0x56     0     Byte field 11 (pField11[0])\n  0x2D    0x57     0     Byte field 11+1\n  0x2E    0x52     0     Byte field 11+2\n  0x2F    0x53     0     Byte field 11+3",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
