      "name": "InitializeLocaleSettings",
      "signature": "void InitializeLocaleSettings(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Initializes locale settings and country ID based on system locale string length and enumeration.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Get length of global locale code string (g_szLocaleCode)\n  2. Set g_bLocaleIs3Char flag: TRUE if length == 3, FALSE otherwise\n  3. If length == 3: set g_dwCountryId to 0x2 (predefined for 3-char codes)\n  4. Otherwise: call FUN_00409d00 to compute country ID from locale string\n  5. Enumerate all system locales via EnumSystemLocalesA with callback FUN_00409930\n  6. Check g_dwLocaleValidation flag (0x4 bit): if clear, reset entire flag to 0x0\n\nParameters:\n  None\n\nReturns:\n  None (void)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - 3-character locale codes are pre-mapped to country ID 0x2\n  - Non-3-char codes require custom lookup via FUN_00409d00\n  - Locale validation flag bit 0x4 can invalidate entire flag when not set",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
