      "name": "FormatNumericValue",
      "signature": "void FormatNumericValue(int nValue, dword cchWidth, int * pbBuffer, dword * pcbRemaining)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Formats an integer value as right-aligned ASCII decimal digits in output buffer.\n\n  Algorithm:\n  1. Check global separator state (g_dwCurrentCharSeparator)\n  2. If separator set, delegate to alternative formatter FUN_0040a71c\n  3. Otherwise proceed with standard digit formatting:\n    a. Validate cchWidth fits in remaining buffer (param_4)\n    b. Extract digits from right to left via modulo 10\n    c. Write each digit as ASCII ('0'-'9') at buffer[cchWidth-1..0]\n    d. Increment digit counter (local_8)\n    e. Divide nValue by 10 for next digit\n  4. Update buffer pointer by digits written\n  5. Decrement remaining size by digits written\n\n  Parameters:\n    nValue - Integer value to format (can be negative, uses lower bits only)\n    cchWidth - Number of digit positions to fill\n    pbBuffer - Pointer to output buffer pointer (double-indirect, *pbBuffer is write position)\n    pcbRemaining - Pointer to remaining buffer size in bytes\n\n  Returns:\n    void - modifies buffer position via *pbBuffer, size via *pcbRemaining\n\n  Special Cases:\n    - If g_dwCurrentCharSeparator != 0: delegates to FUN_0040a71c (conditional formatting)\n    - If cchWidth >= *pcbRemaining: sets *pcbRemaining to 0 (buffer exhausted), no output\n    - Negative values: only uses lower bits due to signed division by 10 (0xa)",
