      "name": "CountValidLockContextEntities",
      "signature": "int CountValidLockContextEntities(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Wrapper that counts all valid lock context entities in the global table\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calls ProcessLockContextEntities with mode=1 (Count Mode)\n2. Returns count of successfully validated entities\n\nParameters:\nNone - this is a parameterless wrapper\n\nReturns:\nint - Count of entities that passed validation (>= 0)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Empty lock context table returns 0\n- Only entities with active flags (0x83) are counted\n- Failed validations are not counted but do not cause errors\n\nSee Also:\nProcessLockContextEntities() - The underlying implementation with mode parameter",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "NOP",
