      "name": "FreeOsFileHandle",
      "signature": "int FreeOsFileHandle(int nFileDescriptor)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Frees an OS file handle from the CRT file descriptor table and resets standard handles when in console debug mode.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate file descriptor is within valid range (less than g_dwMaxFileHandles)\n2. Calculate I/O entry pointer using descriptor index: row = descriptor >> 5, slot = descriptor & 0x1F\n3. Access entry at g_ppIoInfo[row][slot * 9] (9-byte entry stride)\n4. Verify entry has valid flags (bit 0 set) and is not already invalid (-1)\n5. If g_dwConsoleDebugFlag == 1 (console debug mode):\n   a. Map file descriptor 0/1/2 to STD_INPUT/OUTPUT/ERROR handles\n   b. Call SetStdHandle with NULL to reset the standard handle\n6. Mark file handle as invalid by setting first 4 bytes to -1 (0xFFFFFFFF)\n7. Return 0 on success\n8. On failure, set errno to EBADF (9) and DOS errno to 0, return -1\n\nParameters:\n  nFileDescriptor: CRT file descriptor index (0=stdin, 1=stdout, 2=stderr, 3+ user handles)\n\nReturns:\n  int: 0 on success (handle freed), -1 on failure (invalid descriptor or already closed)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - File descriptors 0, 1, 2 get special handling for stdin/stdout/stderr\n  - nStdHandle values: 0xFFFFFFF6 (-10) = STD_INPUT, 0xFFFFFFF5 (-11) = STD_OUTPUT, 0xFFFFFFF4 (-12) = STD_ERROR\n  - Entry stride is 9 bytes (36 bytes per row, 4 handles per row)\n  - Console debug mode resets Windows standard handles to NULL\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0xFFFFFFFF: Invalid handle sentinel value\n  9: EBADF error code (Bad file descriptor)\n  0xFFFFFFF6: STD_INPUT_HANDLE constant\n  0xFFFFFFF5: STD_OUTPUT_HANDLE constant\n  0xFFFFFFF4: STD_ERROR_HANDLE constant",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:e49319598ce25b712e5d6f6d5281c3d3662f1dda6723371c97d8bf62712cd0dd",
