      "name": "FlushOutputBuffer",
      "signature": "int FlushOutputBuffer(FILE * pFile)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Flushes pending output data from a FILE stream buffer to disk.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if file is open for writing (flag & 0x3 == 0x2)\n2. Check if file has buffering enabled (flag & 0x108 != 0)\n3. Calculate bytes to flush: nBytesToFlush = _ptr - _base\n4. If bytes pending > 0, call __lseek to write buffer contents\n5. On success, clear the written flag if set (flag &= ~0x2)\n6. On failure, set error flag (flag |= 0x20) and return -1\n7. Reset buffer: _cnt = 0, _ptr = _base\n8. Return 0 on success\n\nParameters:\n  pFile (FILE*) - Pointer to FILE structure to flush\n\nReturns:\n  int - 0 on success, -1 on write failure\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Returns 0 immediately if file not open for writing\n- Returns 0 immediately if no buffering enabled\n- Returns 0 if buffer is empty (no pending data)\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x2    - _IOWRT: File open for writing\n  0x3    - Mask for read/write mode bits\n  0x20   - _IOERR: I/O error flag\n  0x80   - Sign bit check for clearing write flag\n  0x108  - _IOMYBUF | _IONBF: Buffer allocation flags\n\nStructure Layout (FILE at ESI):\n  Offset  Size  Field   Type    Description\n  0x00    4     _ptr    char*   Current buffer position\n  0x04    4     _cnt    int     Characters remaining in buffer\n  0x08    4     _base   char*   Base of buffer\n  0x0C    4     _flag   int     File status flags\n  0x10    4     _file   int     File descriptor\n\nLibrary: Visual Studio 2003 Release (__flush)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
