      "name": "CloseFileDescriptorLocked",
      "signature": "int CloseFileDescriptorLocked(uint dwFileDescriptor)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Closes a file descriptor and clears its I/O info entry (locked version for thread safety).\n\nVisual Studio 2003 CRT library function. Converts C runtime file descriptor to Windows\nOS handle, closes the handle, and cleans up internal I/O state. Special handling prevents\nclosing stdout (fd=1) when it shares a handle with stderr (fd=2).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get the OS handle for the file descriptor via __get_osfhandle()\n2. If handle is invalid (-1), skip close and go directly to cleanup\n3. For stdout (1) or stderr (2), check if both share the same OS handle\n4. If shared handle detected, skip CloseHandle to avoid breaking other stream\n5. Otherwise, call CloseHandle() on the OS handle\n6. If CloseHandle fails, capture error code via GetLastError()\n7. Call __free_osfhnd() to free the OS handle association\n8. Clear the flags byte in the I/O info structure at index [fd >> 5][fd & 0x1F]\n9. If error occurred, map Windows error to errno via __dosmaperr()\n10. Return 0 on success, -1 on failure\n\nParameters:\n  dwFileDescriptor (uint) - C runtime file descriptor number (0=stdin, 1=stdout, 2=stderr, 3+)\n\nReturns:\n  int - 0 on success, -1 on failure (errno set via __dosmaperr)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - fd 1 and 2 may share same OS handle (console redirection)\n  - Invalid handle (-1) silently succeeds without calling CloseHandle\n  - I/O info entry always cleared regardless of close success\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x24 = 36 bytes per I/O info entry (ioinfo structure size)\n  0x1F = 31 = mask for entry index within block (32 entries per block)\n  0x5  = shift count to get block index (fd >> 5 = fd / 32)\n  0x4  = offset to flags byte within ioinfo structure\n\nStructure Layout (ioinfo - 36 bytes per entry):\n  Offset  Size  Field         Type     Description\n  0x00    4     osfhnd        HANDLE   OS file handle\n  0x04    1     osfile        byte     File status flags (cleared to 0 on close)\n  0x05    1     pipech        byte     Pipe lookahead character\n  0x06    2     padding       ushort   Alignment padding\n  0x08    28    reserved      byte[28] Reserved/internal use\n\nError Handling:\n  - GetLastError() called only if CloseHandle() returns FALSE\n  - __dosmaperr() translates Windows error to C errno\n  - Returns -1 and sets errno for any close failure",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
