      "name": "CloseFileDescriptor",
      "signature": "int CloseFileDescriptor(int nFileHandle)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Closes a file descriptor and releases associated resources.\n\nCRT library function implementing __close() from MSVC runtime. Validates the file\ndescriptor, acquires a lock, closes the underlying OS handle, and releases the lock.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate file handle is within valid range (< g_dwMaxFileHandles)\n2. Check if file descriptor is in use (flag bit 0x1 set)\n3. Lock the file handle for thread-safe access\n4. Re-verify descriptor is still valid after acquiring lock\n5. If valid, call CloseFileDescriptorLocked to close the OS handle\n6. If invalid after lock (race condition), set errno to EBADF (9)\n7. Unlock the file handle\n8. Return result code\n\nParameters:\n- nFileHandle (int): File descriptor index to close (0 = stdin, 1 = stdout, 2 = stderr)\n\nReturns:\n- 0: Success - file descriptor closed and resources released\n- -1: Error - invalid handle or handle not in use (errno set to EBADF = 9)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Thread safety: Uses LockFileHandle/UnlockFileHandleThunk for synchronization\n- Race condition handling: Re-checks validity after acquiring lock\n- EBADF (9) set when handle invalid or not in use\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n- 0x1: File descriptor in-use flag (ioinfo.osflags bit 0)\n- 0x9: EBADF errno value (Bad file descriptor)\n- 0x1f (31): Mask for index within ioinfo block (32 entries per block)\n- 5: Right shift to get block index (divide by 32)\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset  Size  Field         Type    Description\n0x00    4     osfhnd        HANDLE  OS file handle\n0x04    1     osflags       byte    File descriptor flags (bit 0 = in use)\n0x05    1     pipech        byte    Pipe character buffer\n0x06    2     padding       -       Alignment padding\n0x08    4     lockinitflag  uint    Lock initialization flag\n(Each ioinfo entry is 9 DWORDs = 36 bytes)\n\nLibrary: Visual Studio 2003 Release (__close)",
