      "name": "ValidateAsyncEventInit",
      "signature": "void ValidateAsyncEventInit(GameSessionConfig * pSessionConfig)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Validates async event listener initialization and container data integrity.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if ContainerData pointer (ESI) is valid; abort with 0x87 if null\n2. Call InitializeAsyncEventListeners with config and event handle slot\n3. If init returns 0 (failure): copy data via SafeCopyDataWithLocking and abort with 0x8f\n4. If init returns non-zero: compare expected handle (EDI) with returned handle\n5. If handles match, return successfully; otherwise abort with 0x92\n\nParameters:\n  pSessionConfig (GameSessionConfig *) - Configuration for the game session\n  IMPLICIT ESI (ContainerData *) - Container data object to validate\n  IMPLICIT EDI (uint) - Expected event handle value for validation\n\nReturns:\n  void - Returns only on success (handle validation passes)\n  Calls CleanupAndAbort on all error paths (does not return)\n\nError Codes:\n  0x87 (135) - Null container data pointer\n  0x8f (143) - Async event initialization returned failure\n  0x92 (146) - Event handle mismatch after successful init\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x104 (260) - Buffer size for SafeCopyDataWithLocking\n  0x6fc0d2e9 - Error code for CleanupAndAbort\n  0xffffffff (-1) - ReportError exit code\n\nCallers: OpenAndValidateResource, InitGameSessionConfig\nCallees: InitializeAsyncEventListeners, SafeCopyDataWithLocking, GetReturnAddress, CleanupAndAbort, ReportError",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
      "method": "NOP",
