      "name": "InitGameSessionConfig",
      "signature": "GameSessionConfig * InitGameSessionConfig(int nInputHandle, int * pnResourceCount)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Initializes a game session configuration by loading container data and allocating a GameSessionConfig structure.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calls GetDefaultResourceCount with implicit EAX parameter to retrieve container data\n2. If operation fails, calls GetLastError and ValidateParameterOrShutdown, then returns NULL\n3. Validates container pointer is non-null, else aborts with error 0x6fc0d2e9 at line 0x59\n4. Calls GetDefaultResourceCount again to initialize temporary buffer\n5. If second retrieval fails, copies container data to szFilePath buffer for error reporting, then aborts at line 0x5f\n6. Allocates GameSessionConfig structure via Ordinal_10042 (SMemAlloc) with size 0xcf and flag 0\n7. If allocation fails, returns NULL\n8. Initializes the config structure via FUN_6fc07c60\n9. Validates container pointer again, else aborts at line 0x49\n10. Calls BuildProjectPathThunk to set up project paths\n11. If pnResourceCount is non-null, stores the result count\n12. Returns the allocated GameSessionConfig pointer\n\nParameters:\n  nInputHandle (int) - IMPLICIT via EAX: Handle or identifier passed to GetDefaultResourceCount\n  pnResourceCount (int *) - Optional output parameter to receive resource count result\n\nReturns:\n  GameSessionConfig * - Pointer to initialized config on success, NULL on failure\n\nError Handling:\n  Line 0x59 (89): Container data NULL after initial retrieval\n  Line 0x5f (95): Second GetDefaultResourceCount call failed\n  Line 0x49 (73): Container NULL before BuildProjectPathThunk\n  All errors trigger CleanupAndAbort with error code 0x6fc0d2e9\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0xcf (207) - Size parameter for Ordinal_10042 (SMemAlloc) allocation\n  0x104 (260) - MAX_PATH buffer size for szFilePath\n  0x320 - Offset into container structure passed to Ordinal_10042\n\nOrdinal References:\n  Ordinal_10042 = SMemAlloc (Storm.dll) - Memory allocation, called at 0x6fc07f76\n\nCallers:\n  FUN_6fc09410, LoadSystemCharacterMap, Ordinal_10006, Ordinal_10009\n\nNote: abTempBuffer is a 4-byte stack temporary used for GetDefaultResourceCount output",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
