      "name": "GetUtf8CharacterByteCount",
      "signature": "int GetUtf8CharacterByteCount(int nMaxBytes)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Calculates the byte length of a single UTF-8 encoded character.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate nMaxBytes >= 1, return -1 if invalid\n2. Load lead byte from implicit EAX pointer and initialize codepoint accumulator\n3. Iterate through UTF-8 decode table (g_aUtf8DecodeTable):\n   a. If table mask is 0, return -1 (no matching UTF-8 pattern)\n   b. Increment bytes consumed counter\n   c. Apply mask to lead byte and compare with expected pattern\n   d. If pattern matches:\n      - Apply value mask to extract codepoint bits\n      - Validate codepoint >= minimum value (reject overlong encodings)\n      - Return bytes consumed count on success\n   e. If max bytes exceeded, return -1 (truncated sequence)\n   f. Read next continuation byte, XOR with 0x80\n   g. Validate continuation byte pattern (bits 7-6 must be 0)\n   h. Accumulate 6-bit payload: shift left 6, OR new bits\n   i. Advance to next table entry (stride 16 bytes)\n4. Return -1 on invalid continuation byte\n\nParameters:\n  pbSrcBytes (EAX) - byte*: IMPLICIT. Pointer to UTF-8 encoded byte sequence\n  nMaxBytes (stack) - int: Maximum bytes available to read from source\n\nReturns:\n  >= 1: Number of bytes consumed (1-4 for valid modern UTF-8, up to 6 for legacy)\n  -1: Error - invalid sequence, truncated, or overlong encoding\n\nUTF-8 Decode Table Structure (g_aUtf8DecodeTable at 0x6fc102e8):\n  Offset  Size  Field        Description\n  0x0     2     wMask        Lead byte mask for pattern matching\n  0x2     2     wPattern     Expected pattern after masking\n  0x4     4     dwValueMask  Mask to extract codepoint bits\n  0x8     4     reserved     Unused padding\n  0xC     4     nMinValue    Minimum valid codepoint for this length\n\nUTF-8 Encoding Patterns:\n  1-byte: 0xxxxxxx (0x00-0x7F) - ASCII compatible\n  2-byte: 110xxxxx 10xxxxxx (0xC0-0xDF lead)\n  3-byte: 1110xxxx 10xxxxxx 10xxxxxx (0xE0-0xEF lead)\n  4-byte: 11110xxx 10xxxxxx 10xxxxxx 10xxxxxx (0xF0-0xF7 lead)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x80: XOR mask converting continuation byte 10xxxxxx to 00xxxxxx\n  0xC0: AND mask to validate continuation byte (result must be 0)\n  0x10: Table entry stride (16 bytes per entry)\n  6: Shift amount for 6-bit continuation payload\n\nNote: Similar to DecodeUtf8Character but returns only byte count, not codepoint.",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:0e2fafbd66798284da29812af52990c33a1e4a3effb0bfba557af776a77a0291",
