      "name": "EncodeUtf8Character",
      "signature": "int EncodeUtf8Character(ushort wCodePoint)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Encodes a single Unicode code point to UTF-8 bytes.\n\nLooks up the code point in g_aUtf8DecodeTable to determine:\n  - Number of bytes needed (1-4 for valid UTF-8)\n  - Lead byte prefix mask\n  - Bit shift amount for encoding\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize byte counter to 0\n2. Iterate through g_aUtf8DecodeTable entries\n3. For each entry, increment byte count and check if code point fits range\n4. If code point <= entry max value:\n   a. Encode lead byte: (codepoint >> shift) | prefix_mask\n   b. Encode continuation bytes: ((codepoint >> shift) & 0x3F) | 0x80\n   c. Decrement shift by 6 for each continuation byte\n5. Return byte count on success, -1 if code point not encodable\n\nParameters:\n  wCodePoint - Unicode code point to encode (ushort, 0x0000-0xFFFF)\n  IMPLICIT in_EAX (pbDestBuffer) - Pointer to destination buffer for UTF-8 bytes\n\nReturns:\n  int - Number of bytes written (1-4), or -1 on encoding failure\n\nCallers: utfnwidth, utfwidth, toUtf\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x3F (00111111) - Mask for 6-bit continuation byte data\n  0x80 (10000000) - UTF-8 continuation byte prefix\n  6 - Bits per continuation byte",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
      "method": "NOP",
