      "name": "ContainsWideCharInAnsi",
      "signature": "uint ContainsWideCharInAnsi(void * this, char * szAnsiString, ushort * pwSearchChar)",
      "calling_convention": "__thiscall",
      "return_type": "uint",
      "comment": "Checks if a wide character exists within an ANSI string converted to wide characters.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize 21-element wide char buffer on stack with zeros\n2. Convert ANSI string (from this pointer) to wide chars (5 bytes per loop iteration)\n3. Process up to 20 characters maximum (0x14), breaking on null terminator\n4. Null-terminate the wide string at appropriate position\n5. Count length of resulting wide string\n6. Linear search through wide buffer for matching character\n7. Return 1 if character found, 0 otherwise\n\nParameters:\n  this (ECX) - Pointer to ANSI source string\n  pwSearchChar - Pointer to wide character to search for\n\nReturns:\n  uint - 1 (TRUE) if character found, 0 (FALSE) otherwise\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x14 (20) - Maximum character count for conversion\n  21 - Wide buffer size (20 chars + null terminator)\n  5 - Characters processed per unrolled loop iteration\n\nNotes:\n  - Loop is unrolled 5x for performance optimization\n  - Wide buffer uses 1-based indexing (index 0 unused)\n  - CONCAT31 return path preserves upper bytes while setting result to 1\n  - SSA variables iVar1/puVar2/uVar3 are decompiler-generated temporaries",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
