      "name": "CheckLastCharInPattern",
      "signature": "bool CheckLastCharInPattern(char * lpszPattern)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "uint",
      "comment": "Checks if the last character of a wide-string matches any character in an ANSI pattern.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Convert ANSI pattern string to wide-char buffer (max 20 chars)\n   - Unrolled loop processes 5 chars per iteration for efficiency\n   - Terminates on null or max length\n2. Count converted pattern length via pointer walk\n3. Get wide-string length via pointer walk (null check)\n4. Compare last char of wide-string against each pattern char\n5. Return true on first match, false if no match\n\nParameters:\n  lpszPattern (char*, ECX): ANSI character set to check against (e.g., \"aeiou\")\n  IMPLICIT pwszString (wchar_t*, ESI): Wide-string to check last character of\n\nReturns:\n  bool - true if last char of pwszString matches any char in lpszPattern\n         false if no match or empty strings\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Null pwszString: nIndex remains 0, comparison at [-1] may be undefined\n  - Pattern > 20 chars: Truncated to 20 characters\n  - Empty pattern: Returns false (nPatternLen == 0)\n\nUsage Context:\n  Called from Unicode::Personalize to determine possessive suffix rules\n  based on whether name ends with vowel (aeiou pattern check)\n\nStack Frame Layout:\n  Offset  Size  Field             Type         Description\n  -0x2A   42    awPatternBuffer   ushort[21]   Wide-char pattern buffer\n",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
