      "name": "GetLanguageIdByCode",
      "signature": "int GetLanguageIdByCode(char * szLangCode)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Looks up a language ID by its three-letter language code string.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize loop index to 0 and pointer to language code table start\n2. Compare input language code with current table entry using case-insensitive comparison\n3. If match found, return corresponding language ID from offset 0x14 of the entry\n4. Advance pointer by 24 bytes (0x18) to next table entry\n5. Increment index counter\n6. Continue loop until pointer exceeds table end address (0x6fc102e8)\n7. Return 0 if no matching language code found\n\nParameters:\n  szLangCode (char*, EBX) - Three-letter ISO language code (e.g., ENG, DEU, FRA)\n\nReturns:\n  int (EAX) - Language ID corresponding to the code, or 0 if not found\n\nGlobals Referenced:\n  g_ppszLanguageCodeTable (0x6fc101b0) - Array of language entry structures\n  g_anLanguageIdTable (0x6fc101c4) - Language ID values at offset 0x14 in each entry\n\nTable Structure (24 bytes per entry):\n  Offset  Size  Field             Description\n  0x00    4     pszLanguageCode   Pointer to language code string\n  0x04    16    (unknown)         Reserved/other data\n  0x14    4     nLanguageId       Internal language ID value\n\nCalled By:\n  Ordinal_10003 - System language detection function\n\nSee Also:\n  __stricmp - Case-insensitive string comparison",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
      "method": "NOP",
