      "name": "LookupStringKeyInTable",
      "signature": "int LookupStringKeyInTable(void * pTable, char * * ppszStringPointers, char * szKey, int * pnOutStringIdx)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Searches a string hash table for a key and returns the associated string index.\n\nThis function implements open-addressing hash table lookup with linear probing for\nthe Diablo 2 localization system. It searches for a string key in the hash table\nand returns the table index and string pointer if found.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calculate initial hash bucket index via Ordinal_10011 (ELF hash variant)\n2. Compute entries base offset from table header fields\n3. Loop through table entries using linear probing:\n   a. Check if entry at current bucket is occupied (flag == 0x01)\n   b. If occupied, compare stored key against search key byte-by-byte\n   c. On match (strcmp == 0), retrieve string pointer from pointer array\n   d. If string pointer is NULL, trigger fatal error (line 0x298 = 664)\n   e. If not found, advance to next bucket: (bucket + 1) % tableSize\n4. Return entry index on success, or 0xFFFF on failure\n\nParameters:\n  pTable (void*): Pointer to string table structure with layout:\n                +0x02: ushort - Header size / 2 (used for offset calculation)\n                +0x04: uint   - Table size (number of hash buckets)\n                +0x0D: uint   - Maximum entries count (loop bound)\n                +0x15: Start of hash entry array\n  ppszStringPointers (char**): Array of string pointers indexed by bucket\n  szKey (char*): Null-terminated string key to search for\n  pnOutStringIdx (int*): Output parameter receiving the string pointer on match\n\nReturns:\n  Success: Table index in low word, high word from entry[bucket + offset + 1]\n  Failure: 0xFFFFxxxx (high word from last comparison result, low word = 0xFFFF)\n\nHash Entry Structure (17 bytes each, offset by bucket * 0x11):\n  +0x00: byte  - Occupied flag (0x01 = valid entry)\n  +0x07: int   - Offset to key string (relative to pTable base)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x11 = 17 bytes per hash entry\n  0x15 = 21 bytes header offset to entries array\n  0x298 = 664 (source line number for error reporting)\n  0x6fc0d2e9 = Error code constant passed to CleanupAndAbort\n\nError Handling:\n  If matching entry found but string pointer is NULL, calls:\n  GetReturnAddress() -> CleanupAndAbort(0x6fc0d2e9, context, 664) -> ReportError(-1)\n  This is a fatal/unrecoverable error indicating corrupted string table data.",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:b7bf28606a0a6f07f0ffc9c2d37efd2fb03ff64f94a1231bf26c596ac5f26f1a",
