      "name": "CreateAndValidateGameConfig",
      "signature": "GameSessionConfig * CreateAndValidateGameConfig(ushort wExpectedVersion)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "ushort *",
      "comment": "Creates and validates a GameSessionConfig structure from Unicode mapping data.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calls InitGameSessionConfig with global Unicode mapping pointer to allocate config\n2. Invokes Ordinal_10010 to populate/validate header fields from config data\n3. Compares expected version against config field_0 - aborts on mismatch (line 0xD0)\n4. Iterates through config entries (stride 0x11) validating boundary values\n5. Checks each entry's lower bound (offset -4) and upper bound against dwBoundaryValue\n6. Aborts on entry validation failure (line 0xE2 for lower, 0xE3 for upper bound)\n7. Returns validated config pointer on success\n\nParameters:\n- wExpectedVersion (ushort): Expected version number to validate against config header\n\nReturns:\n- GameSessionConfig*: Pointer to initialized and validated configuration structure\n- Never returns on validation failure (calls ReportError(-1))\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Aborts with line 0xD0 if version mismatch\n- Aborts with line 0xE2 if entry lower bound exceeds boundary\n- Aborts with line 0xE3 if entry upper bound exceeds boundary\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n- 0xD0 (208): Line number for version mismatch abort\n- 0xE2 (226): Line number for lower bound validation failure\n- 0xE3 (227): Line number for upper bound validation failure\n- 0x11 (17): Stride between config entries in bytes\n- 0x6fc0d2e9: Error code constant (g_nErrorCode)\n\nStructure Layout (GameSessionConfig accessed offsets):\nOffset  Size  Field             Description\n0x00    2     field_0           Version/type field (low word)\n0x02    2     field_0+2         Entry start index (word at offset 2)\n0x04    4     pGameInstance     Entry count (used as loop bound)\n0x09    4     field_c+1         Boundary value (misaligned read)\n0x11    4     pDataArray+1      Additional boundary data\n0x15+   17*N  pConfigTable[N]   Entry array with 17-byte stride",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
