      "name": "LookupSysToUnicodeCode",
      "signature": "uint LookupSysToUnicodeCode(uint dwUnused, ushort wSysCharCode)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "uint",
      "comment": "Performs binary search to convert a system character code to its Unicode equivalent.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. If wSysCharCode is a control character (< 0x20), return it unchanged\n2. Calculate the upper bound index as map count minus one\n3. Check if wSysCharCode is within the valid range of the sorted mapping table\n4. If equal to highest entry Unicode code, return immediately with that index\n5. Otherwise perform binary search: calculate middle index as half of high bound\n6. Compare wSysCharCode against the Unicode value at g_pSysToUnicodeMap[g_pUnicodeToSysMap[mid]*4]\n7. If less, narrow to lower half; if greater or equal, narrow to upper half\n8. Repeat until range collapses (nHighBound - nLowBound <= 1)\n9. Verify final index matches the target code; return 0xFFFFFFFF if not found\n10. Return the system code at offset +2 from the matching table entry\n\nParameters:\n  dwUnused: Unused parameter (ECX register, passed for __fastcall calling convention)\n  wSysCharCode: 16-bit system character code to look up (DX register)\n\nReturns:\n  uint: The corresponding Unicode code point on success\n  0xFFFFFFFF: If character code is not found in the mapping table\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Control characters (0x00-0x1F) pass through unchanged\n  - Uses g_pUnicodeToSysMap as a sorted index array for binary search\n  - Uses g_pSysToUnicodeMap as the actual mapping table (4 bytes per entry: sys code at +0, unicode at +2)\n  - Called by sys2Unicode to convert multi-byte system encodings to Unicode",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:fdf3e8201b889e5a6247206b8950d024796b7b8b97c4c2302aa322246d3556c5",
