      "name": "IsValidSystemByte",
      "signature": "int IsValidSystemByte(void * pUnused, byte bCharacter)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Validates if a byte character is allowed for system display.\n\nChecks if the given byte value is a printable character that is not\nwithin any disallowed byte range defined in g_pByteRangeTable.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. If byte < 0x20 (control character), return 0 (invalid)\n2. Iterate through byte range pairs [min, max] in g_pByteRangeTable\n3. If byte falls within any range, return 0 (disallowed)\n4. If not in any range, return 1 (allowed)\n\nParameters:\n  pUnused      - [ECX] Unused parameter (fastcall placeholder)\n  bCharacter   - [DL] Byte value to validate\n\nReturns:\n  1 - Character is valid/allowed for display\n  0 - Character is invalid (control char or in disallowed range)\n\nGlobals:\n  g_bByteRangeCount @ 0x6fc10a54 - Number of byte range pairs\n  g_pByteRangeTable @ 0x6fc10a58 - Pointer to array of [min,max] byte pairs\n\nCalled by:\n  sysWidth @ 0x6fc0b50c - Character width calculation\n  unicode2Sys @ 0x6fc0b5cd - Unicode to system encoding conversion\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x1f - Control character threshold (less than 0x20 equals invalid)\n  *2   - Stride for byte range pairs (2 bytes per entry)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:19b46523ebda97f135b50fd6a144881b02f46f8310a9963eac5af5c965e7410c",
