      "name": "InitStringTables",
      "signature": "int InitStringTables(int nLoadExpansion, char * szLocalePath)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Initializes game localization string tables and Unicode conversion system.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if already initialized - if g_pBaseStringTable exists, increment ref count and return\n2. Determine locale: use szLocalePath param if provided, else read from registry\n3. Select charset based on locale: CJK for Korea/Japan, Cyrillic for RUS, LATIN2 for East, LATIN default\n4. Copy charset string to szCharset local buffer\n5. Load font system map via Unicode::loadSysMap from \"data/local/font/{charset}/default.map\"\n6. Load base string table (string.tbl) via LoadAndValidateStringTable\n7. Allocate g_pBaseHashTable (nHashCount * 4 bytes) and zero-initialize\n8. First pass: Calculate total Unicode width for all strings in base table\n9. Allocate g_pwszStringData buffer (nTotalUnicodeChars * 2 bytes)\n10. Second pass: Convert strings to Unicode, populate hash table with pointers\n11. Load patch string table (patchstring.tbl) - assert on failure\n12. Repeat allocation/conversion for patch strings (g_pPatchHashTable, g_pwszPatchStringData)\n13. If nLoadExpansion: Load expansion table (expansionstring.tbl) - assert on failure\n14. Repeat allocation/conversion for expansion strings\n15. Initialize magnitude suffixes from string IDs 0x14D0-0x14D3 (K/M/B/T)\n\nParameters:\n  nLoadExpansion (int): ECX - if non-zero, loads Lord of Destruction expansion strings\n  szLocalePath (char*): EDX - optional locale path override, NULL for registry lookup\n\nReturns:\n  int: 1 on success, 0 if base string table fails to load\n\nString Tables Loaded:\n  - data/local/lng/{locale}/string.tbl (base game strings)\n  - data/local/lng/{locale}/patchstring.tbl (patch strings)\n  - data/local/lng/{locale}/expansionstring.tbl (LoD strings if nLoadExpansion)\n\nGlobals Modified:\n  - g_pBaseStringTable: Pointer to loaded base .tbl file\n  - g_pBaseHashTable: Unicode string pointer array indexed by string ID\n  - g_pwszStringData: Base Unicode string data buffer\n  - g_pPatchStringTable, g_pPatchHashTable, g_pwszPatchStringData: Patch table data\n  - g_pExpansionStringTable, g_pExpansionHashTable, g_pwszExpStringData: Expansion data\n  - g_nStringRefCount: Reference counter for initialization\n  - g_wKiloSuffix, g_wMillionSuffix, g_wBillionsSuffix, g_wTrilSuffix: Magnitude chars\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  - 0x103: MAX_PATH-1 for safe string copy\n  - 0x11: Entry stride in string table (17 bytes per hash entry)\n  - 0xF: Offset to entry data within table header\n  - 0x15: Header size before string data (21 bytes)\n  - 0x14D0-0x14D3: String IDs for K/M/B/T suffixes\n  - 0x4B, 0x4D, 0x42, 0x54: ASCII for K, M, B, T (fallback)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
