      "name": "CloseAndFreeStreamStructures",
      "signature": "int CloseAndFreeStreamStructures(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Closes open file streams and frees stream structure memory.\n\nIterates through the global stream structure table starting at index 3,\nclosing files that have certain flags set (0x83 = read|write|read-write modes).\nFor indices >= 20, also deletes the critical section and deallocates the\nstream structure memory, clearing the table entry.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Acquire critical section 2 (stream table lock)\n2. Loop from index 3 to g_dwStreamStructureCount:\n   a. Get stream structure pointer from g_pStreamStructureTable[index]\n   b. If pointer is valid and file has active flags (0x83):\n      - Call ThreadSafeFileClose on the file\n      - If close succeeded, increment closed count\n   c. If index >= 20:\n      - Delete critical section at structure offset 0x20\n      - Deallocate structure memory\n      - Clear table entry to NULL\n3. Release critical section 2\n4. Return count of successfully closed streams\n\nParameters:\n  None - operates on global stream table\n\nReturns:\n  int - Number of streams that were successfully closed\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x83 - File flag mask (_IOREAD | _IOWRT | _IORW)\n  0x20 - Offset of CRITICAL_SECTION within stream structure\n  3    - First user stream index (0-2 are stdin/stdout/stderr)\n  20   - Index threshold for structure deallocation\n  2    - Critical section index for stream table",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "NOP",
