      "name": "CompareUnicodeCharsCaseInsensitive",
      "signature": "int CompareUnicodeCharsCaseInsensitive(int nUnused1, int nUnused2, ushort wChar1, ushort wChar2)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Compares two Unicode characters case-insensitively using an uppercase conversion table.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. If wChar1 is in ASCII range (< 0x100), look up its uppercase equivalent in _toUpperTable\n2. If wChar2 is in ASCII range (< 0x100), look up its uppercase equivalent in _toUpperTable\n3. Compare the (possibly uppercased) character values\n4. Return 1 if equal, 0 if different\n\nParameters:\n  unused1 (int, ECX) - Unused register parameter (part of struct Unicode calling convention)\n  unused2 (int, EDX) - Unused register parameter (part of struct Unicode calling convention)\n  wChar1 (ushort, Stack+0x04) - First Unicode character to compare\n  wChar2 (ushort, Stack+0x08) - Second Unicode character to compare\n\nReturns:\n  int - 1 if characters match case-insensitively, 0 otherwise\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x100 - ASCII character range boundary (256 characters)\n\nNotes:\n  - Characters outside ASCII range (>= 0x100) are compared without case conversion\n  - Uses _toUpperTable lookup for case conversion (array of ushort, 2 bytes per entry)\n  - Member of Unicode static class (mangled name: ?compare@Unicode@@SIHU1@0@Z)\n  - Ordinal 10022",
