      "name": "ProcessTerminationHandler",
      "signature": "void ProcessTerminationHandler(UINT dwExitCode, int fExecuteAtexitHandlers, int fQuickExit)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "C Runtime process termination handler that orchestrates orderly shutdown of a Windows application.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Acquire critical section lock (ordinal 8) to serialize exit operations\n2. Check g_dwTerminateImmediately - if set, force immediate TerminateProcess()\n3. Set g_dwExitInProgress flag to indicate termination is underway\n4. Store fQuickExit parameter in g_byQuickExitFlag for later access\n5. If fExecuteAtexitHandlers is zero, iterate atexit table backwards calling handlers\n6. Execute pre-terminator initialization table via __initterm()\n7. Always execute post-terminator initialization table via __initterm()\n8. Call VerifyCriticalSectionExitLock() to release lock if appropriate\n9. If fQuickExit is zero, set g_dwTerminateImmediately and call ___crtExitProcess()\n10. Otherwise return for quick exit without full CRT cleanup\n\nParameters:\n  dwExitCode (UINT) - Exit code to pass to operating system (0 = success)\n  fExecuteAtexitHandlers (int) - 0 to execute atexit() handlers, non-zero to skip\n  fQuickExit (int) - Non-zero for quick exit without full CRT cleanup\n\nReturns:\n  void - Does not return if fQuickExit is 0 (calls ___crtExitProcess)\n         Returns only if fQuickExit is non-zero for quick exit path\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If g_dwTerminateImmediately already set, immediately calls TerminateProcess()\n  - Atexit handlers execute in reverse registration order (LIFO)\n  - NULL function pointers in atexit table are skipped\n  - Critical section ordinal 8 serializes all exit operations\n  - Pre/post terminator tables execute regardless of atexit handler flag\n  - SEH exception handler protects entire termination sequence\n\nGlobals Used:\n  g_dwTerminateImmediately (0x6fc105c4) - DWORD flag for immediate termination\n  g_dwExitInProgress (0x6fc105c0) - DWORD flag indicating exit is active\n  g_byQuickExitFlag (0x6fc105bc) - BYTE flag for quick exit mode\n  g_pOnExitTableBase (0x6fc11e30) - Pointer to start of atexit function table\n  g_pOnExitTableEnd (0x6fc11e2c) - Pointer to current position in atexit table\n  g_pPreTerminatorTable (0x6fc0f028) - Pointer to pre-terminator init table\n  g_pPostTerminatorTable (0x6fc0f030) - Pointer to post-terminator init table",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
