      "name": "CompareMemory",
      "signature": "int CompareMemory(void * pBuf1, void * pBuf2, uint dwSize)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Compares two memory blocks byte-by-byte and returns their ordering relationship.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if size is zero - return 0 immediately if so\n2. Check buffer alignment: if both buffers are 4-byte aligned (addresses AND 3 == 0):\n   a. Process in DWORD (4-byte) chunks using CMPSD.REPE (dwSize >> 2 iterations)\n   b. If mismatch found, compare individual bytes within the mismatched DWORD\n   c. Compare remaining bytes (dwSize AND 3) individually\n3. If not aligned or one buffer is not aligned:\n   a. If size is odd, compare first byte separately\n   b. Compare remaining bytes in pairs (2 bytes at a time)\n4. For each comparison, track whether buffer1 < buffer2\n5. Return: -1 if buf1 < buf2, 0 if equal, +1 if buf1 > buf2\n\nParameters:\n  pBuf1 (void*) - Pointer to first memory block to compare\n  pBuf2 (void*) - Pointer to second memory block to compare\n  dwSize (uint) - Number of bytes to compare\n\nReturns:\n  int - Comparison result:\n    -1: First buffer is less than second buffer\n     0: Buffers are equal\n    +1: First buffer is greater than second buffer\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Size of 0 returns 0 immediately (no comparison performed)\n  - Aligned buffers use optimized DWORD comparison (4x faster)\n  - Final result calculated as: (1 - fLessThan) - (fLessThan != 0)\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x3 - Alignment mask for 4-byte boundary check\n  0xff0000 - Mask for third byte in DWORD\n  0x18 - Bit shift for fourth byte (24 bits)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
      "method": "NOP",
