      "name": "__unlock_file",
      "signature": "void __unlock_file(FILE * pFile)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Releases lock on a FILE stream.\n\nInternal CRT function that unlocks a file stream after I/O operations complete.\nHandles two distinct memory regions: internal _iob file table entries and\nexternally allocated FILE structures with embedded critical sections.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load FILE* parameter from stack\n2. Compare against internal _iob table lower bound (0x6fc0f7f0)\n3. If below lower bound, take external critical section path\n4. Compare against internal _iob table upper bound (0x6fc0fa50)\n5. If above upper bound, take external critical section path\n6. INTERNAL PATH: Calculate critical section index from FILE* offset\n   - Index = ((pFile - 0x6fc0f7f0) >> 5) + 0x10\n   - Call AcquireCriticalSectionByIndex to release indexed lock\n7. EXTERNAL PATH: Calculate embedded CRITICAL_SECTION address\n   - pCritSect = pFile + 0x20\n   - Call LeaveCriticalSection directly\n\nParameters:\n- pFile (FILE*): Pointer to FILE stream to unlock\n  Must be a valid FILE* from fopen/freopen or internal _iob array\n\nReturns:\n- void: No return value. Function always succeeds if pFile valid.\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x6fc0f7f0: Base address of internal _iob file table\n- 0x6fc0fa50: End address of internal _iob file table\n- 0x20: Offset to embedded CRITICAL_SECTION in FILE structure\n- 0x10: Base critical section index for internal files\n- >>5: Division by 32 (sizeof FILE entry in _iob array)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Internal files (stdin/stdout/stderr and _iob entries): Use indexed CS\n- External files (heap-allocated FILE): Use embedded CRITICAL_SECTION",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
      "method": "NOP",
