      "name": "__fcloseall",
      "signature": "int __fcloseall(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Closes all open file streams in the CRT file table.\n\nIterates through the global file stream table starting from index 3 (skipping\nstdin, stdout, stderr) and closes each open stream. For streams at index 20\nor higher, also deletes the associated critical section and deallocates memory.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Acquire file table lock via __lock(1)\n2. Iterate from index 3 to g_nFileStreamCount\n3. For each non-null stream pointer:\n   a. Check if stream is active (flag & 0x83 non-zero)\n   b. If active, call _fclose() and increment success counter on success\n   c. If index >= 20 (dynamically allocated):\n      - Delete the critical section at offset 0x20\n      - Deallocate stream memory\n      - Clear table entry\n4. Release file table lock\n5. Return count of successfully closed streams\n\nReturns:\n  int - Number of streams successfully closed (0 if none)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Streams 0-2 (stdin/stdout/stderr) are never closed\n- Streams 3-19 are static and only closed, not deallocated\n- Streams >= 20 are dynamically allocated and fully cleaned up\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n- 0x83: FILE flag mask (_IOREAD | _IOWRT | _IORW)\n- 0x14 (20): First dynamically allocated stream index\n- 0x20 (32): Offset to CRITICAL_SECTION in FILE struct\n\nStructure Layout (FILE):\n  Offset  Size  Field              Type               Description\n  0x00    4     _ptr               char*              Current buffer position\n  0x04    4     _cnt               int                Chars remaining in buffer\n  0x08    4     _base              char*              Buffer base address\n  0x0C    4     _flag              int                File status flags\n  0x10    4     _file              int                File descriptor\n  0x14    4     _charbuf           int                Single char buffer\n  0x18    4     _bufsiz            int                Buffer size\n  0x1C    4     _tmpfname          char*              Temp file name\n  0x20    24    _lock              CRITICAL_SECTION   Thread synchronization\n\nError Handling:\n- _fclose() returning -1 indicates close failure; stream not counted\n- Function continues on individual stream errors",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
      "method": "NOP",
