      "name": "FlushAllFileStreams",
      "signature": "int FlushAllFileStreams(int nFlushMode)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Flushes all open file streams based on specified mode.\n\nThis is an internal CRT helper function called by __flushall. It iterates through all file streams in the global stream table, locking each stream before flushing to ensure thread safety.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Acquire global file lock via __lock(1)\n2. Iterate through all file streams (0 to g_nFileStreamCount)\n3. For each stream: check if non-null and has active flags (0x83 mask)\n4. Lock individual file stream with __lock_file2\n5. Re-verify stream flags after locking (race condition protection)\n6. If nFlushMode==1: flush and count successes\n7. If nFlushMode==0: flush only write streams (flag 0x2), track errors\n8. Unlock each stream via UnlockFileStream\n9. Release global lock via __unlock\n10. Return count or error status based on mode\n\nParameters:\n  nFlushMode (int): Flush mode selector\n    1 = Count successful flushes (for flushall)\n    0 = Track errors only (for fflush(NULL))\n\nReturns:\n  If nFlushMode==1: Count of successfully flushed streams (>=0)\n  If nFlushMode==0: 0 on success, -1 if any flush failed\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x83 = FILE active flags mask (_IOREAD|_IOWRT|_IORW = 0x01|0x02|0x80)\n  0x2  = _IOWRT flag (file open for writing)\n  1    = Lock ID for global file table lock\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Null stream entries are skipped\n  - Streams without active flags (0x83) are skipped\n  - Stream flags are rechecked after locking to handle race conditions\n\nLibrary: Visual Studio 2003 Release (_flsall)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
