      "name": "UnlockFileStream",
      "signature": "undefined UnlockFileStream(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Unlocks a file stream after flush operation.\n\nWrapper function called by flsall after flushing file streams. Uses the ESI register\nas an implicit parameter containing the file stream index, then delegates to\n__unlock_file2 to release the stream lock.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load g_ppFileStreams base pointer from global\n2. Index into array using ESI * 4 to get FILE pointer\n3. Push FILE pointer and index as parameters\n4. Call __unlock_file2 to release the lock\n5. Clean up stack and return\n\nParameters:\n  ESI (IMPLICIT) - File stream index (0-based) into g_ppFileStreams array\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value\n\nGlobals:\n  g_ppFileStreams (DAT_6fc10ab8) - Pointer to array of FILE* stream pointers\n\nCalled By:\n  flsall - After FlushFileAndCheckFlags operations\n\nCalls:\n  __unlock_file2 - Releases critical section lock on file stream\n\nLibrary: Visual Studio 2003 Release (CRT helper)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:c63e0a47ee3cbc6b35e8aef5a27b97d44df4aca5445c943e3639fa8719aae231",
