      "name": "_fclose",
      "signature": "int _fclose(FILE * pFile)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Closes an open file stream and releases associated resources.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize return result to -1 (error default)\n2. Check if file has _IOSTRG flag (0x40) indicating string stream\n3. If NOT a string stream:\n   a. Acquire file lock via __lock_file for thread safety\n   b. Call __fclose_lk to perform actual close operation\n   c. Release file lock via UnlockFileAfterClose\n4. If IS a string stream:\n   a. Clear _flag field to mark stream as closed\n5. Return result code from close operation\n\nParameters:\n  pFile (FILE*) - Pointer to FILE structure to close. Must be valid open stream.\n\nReturns:\n  int - 0 on success, -1 (EOF) on failure\n\nError Handling:\n  Uses SEH prolog/epilog for exception safety. Returns -1 if stream is null\n  or if underlying close fails.\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x40 - _IOSTRG flag: Stream is a string buffer (not backed by file handle)\n  -1   - EOF/Error indicator\n\nThread Safety:\n  Thread-safe. Acquires file lock before close operations on real file streams.\n  String streams (flag 0x40) do not require locking.\n\nRelated Functions:\n  __lock_file - Acquire critical section for file stream\n  __fclose_lk - Locked version performing actual close\n  UnlockFileAfterClose - Release critical section after close",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
      "method": "NOP",
