      "name": "CloseFileArchiveHandle",
      "signature": "void CloseFileArchiveHandle(uint * * ppArchiveHandle@ESI)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Closes and releases a file archive handle, clearing the pointer.\n\nReleases a file archive handle by calling ReleaseFileHandleWithRefCount, then\nclears the pointer to prevent use-after-free. Called during cleanup operations\nsuch as string table unloading in Ordinal_10000.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if the dereferenced pointer (*ppArchiveHandle) is non-NULL\n2. If non-NULL, call ReleaseFileHandleWithRefCount to decrement reference count\n3. Set *ppArchiveHandle = 0 to clear the pointer\n4. Call InitializeModule (Fog thunk, likely FreeMemory) for additional cleanup\n\nParameters:\n  IMPLICIT ppArchiveHandle (uint**@ESI) - Pointer to archive handle pointer\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nNote:\n  The ESI register contains a pointer to the archive handle pointer.\n  This is a D2 custom calling convention. The decompiler shows unaff_ESI\n  because the parameter binding is not fully resolved.\n\nCallers:\n  - Ordinal_10000 (6fc09d50): String table cleanup function",
