      "name": "OpenArchiveFromCdRom",
      "signature": "uint OpenArchiveFromCdRom(uint dwArchiveId, uint * pdwArchiveHandle)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "uint",
      "comment": "Scans all CD-ROM drives to find and open a file archive.\n\nEnumerates logical drives using GetLogicalDriveStringsA, then iterates through\neach drive checking if it is a CD-ROM (drive type 5). For each CD-ROM found,\nconstructs a full path by copying the drive path and appending the source\nfilename (with leading backslashes stripped), then attempts to open the archive.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get all logical drive strings into buffer (max 260 chars)\n2. Strip leading backslashes from source path (in_EAX)\n3. For each drive string in buffer:\n   a. Skip to end of current drive string (find null terminator)\n   b. Check if drive type is CD-ROM (DRIVE_CDROM = 5)\n   c. If CD-ROM: build full path (drive + filename) in ESI buffer\n   d. Attempt to open archive with OpenFileArchive\n   e. If successful, return 1\n   f. Advance to next drive string\n4. Return 0 if no archive found on any CD-ROM\n\nParameters:\n  IMPLICIT in_EAX (char*): Source filename path to search for\n  IMPLICIT unaff_ESI (byte*): Destination buffer for full path construction\n  dwArchiveId (uint): Archive identifier to pass to OpenFileArchive\n  pdwArchiveHandle (uint*): Output pointer for archive handle\n\nReturns:\n  1 - Archive successfully opened from CD-ROM\n  0 - No archive found or error (no drives, GetLogicalDriveStringsA failed)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x104 (260) - MAX_PATH buffer size for drive strings\n  0x5c (92) - Backslash character\n  5 - DRIVE_CDROM drive type constant\n  2 - Archive open flags passed to OpenFileArchive\n  0x7fffffff - Maximum string copy length (INT_MAX)\n\nNote: This function has implicit register parameters via custom calling convention.\nin_EAX contains the source path, ESI contains the output buffer.",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:91b69bad8a37a3e8888853f25a250a9570cb2c6c8a7e8776a626a390f6de91ac",
