      "name": "BindSocketOrAbort",
      "signature": "void BindSocketOrAbort(int nSocketHandle, int nPort, int nFlags)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Attempts to bind a socket to a port, aborting execution on failure.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate ContainerData pointer (ESI) is not NULL\n2. If NULL, set error code 0x70 and abort\n3. Call BindSocketToPortWrapper with socket parameters\n4. If binding succeeds (returns != -1), return normally\n5. If binding fails, copy error data using SafeCopyDataWithLocking\n6. Set error code 0x79 for binding failure\n7. Call CleanupAndAbort with error context and code\n8. Call ReportError(-1) - function does not return\n\nParameters:\n  nSocketHandle (int) - Socket handle for binding operation\n  nPort (int) - Port number to bind to\n  nFlags (int) - Socket binding flags\n  IMPLICIT ESI - ContainerData* pointer to data container\n\nReturns:\n  void - Returns normally only on successful bind\n  Does not return on any error condition\n\nError Codes:\n  0x70 - NULL ContainerData pointer\n  0x79 - Socket binding operation failed\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x104 (260) - Buffer size for error data copy\n  0x6fc0d2e9 - Error context/caller address constant\n  0xffffffff (-1) - Error parameter for ReportError",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
