      "name": "OpenArchiveWithFallback",
      "signature": "uint * OpenArchiveWithFallback(void * this, char * pszPathBuffer, char * pszFilePath)",
      "calling_convention": "__thiscall",
      "return_type": "uint *",
      "comment": "Opens a file archive with fallback path resolution.\n\nAttempts to open an archive file by trying multiple path strategies:\n1. Direct path (use provided path as-is)\n2. Module-relative path (prepend executable directory)\n3. CD-ROM fallback (search CD-ROM drives)\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Copy source path to destination buffer\n2. Try opening archive at provided path\n3. If failed, get module filename and extract directory\n4. Append original filename to module directory\n5. Retry opening archive at new path\n6. If still failed, attempt CD-ROM fallback\n7. Return archive handle on success, NULL on complete failure\n\nParameters:\n    pszPathBuffer (char*, this/ECX): Destination buffer for resolved path (min 260 chars)\n    pszFilePath (char*, Stack+0x4): Source file path to open\n    IMPLICIT in_EAX: Mode flag (0=mode 2, non-zero=mode 3)\n    IMPLICIT EBX: Archive ID to open\n\nReturns:\n    uint*: Pointer to archive handle on success, NULL on failure\n\nMagic Numbers:\n    0x7fffffff - Maximum string copy length (INT_MAX)\n    0x104 (260) - MAX_PATH buffer size\n    0x5c (92) - Backslash character for path parsing\n    0x2, 0x3 - Archive open mode flags\n\nError Handling:\n    Returns NULL if all open attempts fail\n    Clears path buffer to empty string if GetModuleFileName fails",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:8dd959576237e0471e1d12dfe2f8e57fd71b4ee48c9c5345cee22a3fe845572e",
