      "name": "OpenAndValidateResource",
      "signature": "uint OpenAndValidateResource(int nResourceHandle, uint dwFlags, uint dwReserved, GameSessionConfig * pSessionConfig)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "uint",
      "comment": "Opens and validates a resource handle with capacity verification.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call GetDefaultResourceCount to open resource at nResourceHandle\n2. If open fails (result == 0), log error and validate parameter\n3. If resource handle is NULL (0x59), report error and abort\n4. Get actual resource count from the opened resource\n5. If resource count is 0 (0x5f), copy path to buffer and abort\n6. If in_EAX (expected capacity) < actual count (0xa5), abort\n7. Initialize async event listeners via FUN_6fc07c60\n8. Call BuildProjectPathThunk to finalize resource path\n9. Return the expected capacity value (in_EAX)\n\nParameters:\n  nResourceHandle: int - Handle to the resource to open (ECX)\n  dwFlags: uint - Flags for resource opening (EDX, unused in body)\n  dwReserved: uint - Reserved parameter (Stack[0x4], unused)\n  pSessionConfig: GameSessionConfig* - Session configuration for event listeners (Stack[0x8])\n  IMPLICIT in_EAX: uint - Expected capacity/size for validation\n\nReturns:\n  uint: Returns in_EAX (expected capacity) on success\n  Does not return on failure - calls ReportError(-1)\n\nError Codes:\n  0x59 (89): NULL resource handle after open\n  0x5f (95): Resource count is zero\n  0xa5 (165): Capacity insufficient (in_EAX < resource count)\n  0x49 (73): NULL resource handle after event initialization",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:2fd374b1aa428883b94a40b36cd6c7cc0b22b93b5378181da15c1f0850c9dc40",
