      "name": "UpdateCrc16",
      "signature": "void UpdateCrc16(void * this, byte bData)",
      "calling_convention": "__thiscall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Updates a CRC-16 checksum by processing one byte of data using a lookup table.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract high byte of current CRC value from *this\n2. XOR high byte with input byte to compute table index\n3. Shift current CRC left by 8 bits (low byte becomes high byte, low byte zeroed)\n4. XOR shifted value with 16-bit entry from g_awCrc16Table[index]\n5. Store result back to *this\n\nParameters:\n- this (ushort*): Pointer to running CRC-16 accumulator (via ECX, __thiscall)\n- bData (byte): Next byte to incorporate into checksum\n\nReturns:\n- void (modifies *this in place)\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n- 0x8: Shift count for byte extraction (bits 8-15)\n- 0x2: Stride multiplier for 16-bit table entries (2 bytes each)\n\nStructure Layout (CRC-16 table at g_awCrc16Table):\nOffset | Size | Field       | Type   | Description\n0x000  | 2    | entry[0]    | ushort | CRC polynomial term for index 0\n0x002  | 2    | entry[1]    | ushort | CRC polynomial term for index 1\n...    | 2    | entry[255]  | ushort | CRC polynomial term for index 255\n(Total: 512 bytes / 256 entries)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
