      "name": "CompareSysToUnicodeEntry",
      "signature": "int CompareSysToUnicodeEntry(SysToUnicodeEntry * pEntry1, SysToUnicodeEntry * pEntry2)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "CompareSysToUnicodeEntry - Comparator function for qsort/bsearch operations\n\nCompares two SysToUnicodeEntry structures by their Unicode codepoint values.\nUsed as callback for binary search and sorting operations on Unicode lookup tables.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Read the Unicode codepoint (16-bit) from first entry at offset +2\n2. Read the Unicode codepoint (16-bit) from second entry at offset +2\n3. Return difference (negative if first < second, zero if equal, positive if first > second)\n\nParameters:\n  pEntry1 (SysToUnicodeEntry*): Pointer to first SysToUnicodeEntry structure\n  pEntry2 (SysToUnicodeEntry*): Pointer to second SysToUnicodeEntry structure\n\nReturns:\n  int: Comparison result for qsort/bsearch\n       < 0: First entry Unicode value is less than second\n       = 0: Unicode values are equal\n       > 0: First entry Unicode value is greater than second\n\nStructure Layout (SysToUnicodeEntry):\n  Offset  Size  Field         Type    Description\n  0x00    2     wSysCode      ushort  System code value\n  0x02    2     wUnicode      ushort  Unicode codepoint\n\nCallers:\n  - ConvertSysCodeToUnicode (bsearch comparator)\n  - sysWidth (bsearch comparator)  \n  - unicode2Sys (bsearch comparator)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
      "method": "NOP",
