      "name": "ConvertSysCodeToUnicode",
      "signature": "uint ConvertSysCodeToUnicode(ushort wSysCharCode)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "uint",
      "comment": "Converts a system character code to its Unicode equivalent using binary search.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. If wSysCharCode is a control character (< 0x20), return it unchanged\n2. Build 4-byte search key from wSysCharCode in upper word and param in lower word\n3. Perform binary search in g_pSysToUnicodeMap table using bsearch()\n4. If no match found, return 0xFFFFFFFF (INVALID_UNICODE)\n5. Return the Unicode code point from the matched entry\n\nParameters:\n  wSysCharCode (CX): 16-bit system character code to look up\n  IMPLICIT in_AX: Upper 16 bits of the search key (system encoding value)\n\nReturns:\n  uint: Unicode code point on success\n  0xFFFFFFFF: If character code is not found in mapping table\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Control characters (0x00-0x1F) pass through unchanged\n  - Uses g_pSysToUnicodeMap for character mapping lookup\n  - Uses g_wCharMapEntryCount as the number of table entries\n  - Entry format: 4 bytes per entry (system code at +0, Unicode at +2)\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x20 - First non-control ASCII character (space)\n  0xFFFFFFFF - Invalid/not found sentinel value\n  4 - Size of each mapping table entry in bytes\n\nRelated Functions:\n  CompareSysToUnicodeEntry (6fc0afc0) - bsearch comparison callback\n  LookupSysToUnicodeCode (6fc0aff2) - Similar lookup with different search strategy\n  LoadSystemCharacterMap (6fc0b0c0) - Initializes the mapping tables",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
      "method": "NOP",
