      "comment": "Printf-style format string processor - core formatting engine for vsprintf/vsnprintf\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load and validate stack canary (XOR seed with frame pointer for overflow detection)\n2. Initialize local buffers: character conversion buffer (467 bytes), wide char buffer, output state\n3. Load first character from format string and enter main processing loop\n4. While format string character is not null terminator:\n   a) For regular ASCII characters (not %): output directly through WriteCharToStream callback\n   b) For % character: reset format specification flags and enter state machine parser\n   c) Parse format flags (-, +, space, #, 0) via lookup table until non-flag found\n   d) Parse field width as decimal digits (or * to read width from va_list argument)\n   e) Parse precision (.digits or .*) for string/float truncation and padding control\n   f) Parse length modifiers (h for short, l for long, I64 for 64-bit, w for wide char)\n   g) Parse conversion specifier and dispatch to type-specific handler (d,i,o,x,X,u,f,F,e,E,g,G,c,s,p,n)\n5. Extract argument from va_list based on length modifier and pointer advancement\n6. Convert argument to string representation:\n   - Integers: use __aulldvrm for radix conversion (division loop), handles 32/64-bit signed/unsigned\n   - Floats: call __cfltcvt with precision, use __forcdecpt for # flag, __cropzeros for g/G format\n   - Strings: copy bytes/wide chars to buffer until null terminator, handle NULL pointer cases\n   - Characters: convert single char or wide char using _wctomb if wide modifier set\n   - Pointers: format as hex (base 16) with 0x prefix if # flag set\n   - %n specifier: store character count output to pointer argument (short or int based on h flag)\n7. Calculate padding requirements: compare field width against sign length and string length\n8. Apply formatting to convert value to final output string:\n   - Write leading space padding if left-align not set and no zero-pad flag\n   - Write sign/prefix characters (+, -, space for numbers; 0x for hex)\n   - Write zero padding if zero-pad flag set and not left-aligned\n   - Write formatted string/number/character value\n   - Write trailing space padding if left-align flag set\n9. Output final formatted string through write_string/WriteCharRepeatCount callbacks\n10. Loop to next format character and repeat until null terminator found\n11. Perform stack canary validation: XOR canary with frame pointer again, call VerifyStackCanary\n12. Return to caller (vsprintf/vsnprintf functions)\n\nParameters:\n- outputContext: Opaque uint context passed to output callback functions (stream handle, buffer state, etc.)\n- formatString: Null-terminated byte string containing printf format codes and literal characters\n- argList: Pointer to va_list array containing arguments (each 4 or 8 bytes depending on conversion type)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No direct return value; all output passed to registered callback functions",
