      "name": "ReportSecurityError",
      "signature": "void ReportSecurityError(int errorCode)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Displays C runtime security error dialog and terminates the process.\\n\\nAlgorithm:\\n1. Check if custom exception handler installed at DAT_00990924\\n2. If handler exists, call it with error code and target address\\n3. Otherwise, determine error type (buffer overrun vs unknown security error)\\n4. Get module filename using GetModuleFileNameA API\\n5. Build formatted error message with program name and error description\\n6. Display message box with formatted error text and title\\n7. Call exit() with code 3 to terminate the process\\n\\nParameters:\\n  errorCode: Type of security error (1=buffer overrun detected, other=unknown)\\n\\nReturns:\\n  void (function never returns, calls exit() to terminate)\\n\\nSpecial Cases:\\n  - If GetModuleFileNameA fails, uses default &quot;&lt;program_name_unknown&gt;&quot;\\n  - Truncates module filename if combined message exceeds 60 chars\\n  - Uses XOR cookie at [0x0098f308] for stack canary verification\\n  - Calls CRT message box via ___crtMessageBoxA API\\n  - Always exits with code 3 regardless of custom handler\\n\\nError Messages:\\n  Buffer overrun: &quot;Buffer_overrun_detected&quot; + details from 0x0098cf60\\n  Unknown error: &quot;Unknown_security_failure_detecte&quot; + details from 0x0098d020",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
