      "name": "GetOperationDataByType",
      "signature": "void GetOperationDataByType(char * pOutputBuffer, int nDataType)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Retrieves operation data by type from a global configuration table.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if system is initialized; if not, initialize system state and operation counter\n2. Validate that no abort flag is set; exit if flag is non-zero\n3. Search the operation table for an entry matching the current operation counter\n4. Based on nDataType, retrieve and copy the corresponding data to pOutputBuffer:\n   - Type 1: Copy string from table entry at offset +0x18 (PTR_DAT_0098fdb8)\n   - Type 2: Copy string from table entry at offset +0x1C (PTR_DAT_0098fdbc)\n   - Type 3: Copy 32-bit value from table entry at offset +0x20 (DAT_0098fdc0)\n   - Type 4 (default): Copy string from table entry at offset +0x14 (PTR_DAT_0098fdb4)\n\nParameters:\n- pOutputBuffer: Destination buffer for output data (string or 32-bit value)\n- nDataType: Type of data to retrieve (1=type1_string, 2=type2_string, 3=type3_dword, 4+=default_string)\n\nReturns:\n- void; data written to pOutputBuffer\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If operation_counter >= 0x0D, operation_counter is reset to 0\n- If no matching operation found in table, operationIndex defaults to 0\n- Table entries are 0x18 (24) bytes apart, indicating 6 dword fields per entry\n- Table spans from 0x0098FDC4 to 0x0098FEFC (13 maximum entries)",
