      "name": "CleanupGameStateHandlers",
      "signature": "void CleanupGameStateHandlers(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Cleanup Game State Handlers - Performs final shutdown and cleanup of all game handler subsystems when reference counter reaches zero. Responsible for releasing all handler pointers, clearing linked list chains, and invoking module cleanup for all active handler systems.\\n\\nAlgorithm:\\n1. Check if default_handler_enabled flag is set and decrement the reference counter DAT_00990a88\\n2. If counter reaches zero, proceed with cleanup; otherwise exit early\\n3. Cleanup default handler subsystem (offsets 0x32b, 0x330) and clear pointer at 0x990a74\\n4. Cleanup primary handler system (offset 0x123) and clear main handler pointer at 0x990a64\\n5. If medium_range_handler_ptr is non-null, cleanup medium range handler (offset 0x33e) and clear it\\n6. If DAT_00990a78 is non-null, cleanup associated resource (offset 0x343)\\n7. Cleanup secondary handler system (offset 0x123) and clear enabled flag at 0x990a70\\n8. If high_range_handler_ptr is non-null, cleanup high range handler (offset 0x34c)\\n9. If DAT_00990a7c is non-null, cleanup associated resource (offset 0x351)\\n10. Check if high_range_handler_enabled is set, cleanup (offset 0x123) if needed\\n11. Traverse linked list starting at DAT_00990a60 and cleanup each node (offsets 0x379, 0x37a, 0x37b)\\n12. Clear the linked list head pointer at 0x990a60\\n13. Call unloadSysMap() to unload system map resources\\n14. Return from function\\n\\nParameters:\\nNone - operates on global handler state variables\\n\\nReturns:\\nvoid - no return value, function performs side effects on global state\\n\\nSpecial Cases:\\nReference counter DAT_00990a88 controls whether cleanup actually executes. Multiple entities can hold references, and cleanup only runs when counter reaches zero. Linked list cleanup is safe against null pointers (DAT_00990a60 is checked before loop). Magic number offsets (0x32b, 0x330, 0x123, etc.) represent module IDs for cleanup operations.",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "API",
      "index": "API:90f0058b5f3cba0fc3497935fa799600",
