      "name": "ResolveDataHandler",
      "signature": "uint ResolveDataHandler(byte * pData)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Resolves data through registered handler chains.\n\nQueries the provided data pointer through medium-range, high-range, and default handler chains to obtain a resolved value. This wrapper function initializes the output parameter and delegates to the core handler resolution logic.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize result value to 0\n2. Call handler resolution function with data pointer and result output parameter\n3. Return resolved value from output parameter\n\nParameters:\n- pData (byte*): Data pointer to resolve through handler chains\n\nReturns:\nuint: Resolved value from handler chains, or 0 if initialization fails. Values from medium-range handlers are offset by 10000, high-range by 20000.\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Null pointer handling delegated to handler chain\n- Default value of 0 returned on initialization failure\n- Handler offsets ensure unique identification of handler source",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:7e2e82b0a2e7c375a6455546f5e7fb2e",
